<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brasidas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 422 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brasidas was a Spartan general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>. In 424 BCE he marched through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcidice">Chalcidice</a>, where he won over Athenian allies and captured Amphipolis. He was killed in 422 BCE defending Amphipolis in the battle where the Athenian leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleon">Cleon</a> also died, and the city honoured him as its founder.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brasidas.jpg" alt="Brasidas" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Walter Crane · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:He_became_a_target_for_every_arrow_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
